 network market share in South Korea. Source: The Ministry of Science and ICT (MSIT) (2023).","target":"https://blog.apnic.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Korea-fig4.jpg","line":56,"embedded":true},{"title":"Figure 5 — Mobile network market share in South Korea. Source: The Ministry of Science and ICT (MSIT) (2023).","target":"https://blog.apnic.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Korea-fig5.jpg","line":64,"embedded":true},{"title":"Figure 6 — Current status of 5G networks in South Korea.","target":"https://blog.apnic.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Korea-fig6.jpg","line":74,"embedded":true},{"title":"Figure 7 — Current status of 5G networks in South Korea.","target":"https://blog.apnic.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Korea-fig7.jpg","line":84,"embedded":true},{"title":"Figure 8 — Interconnection structure of South Korean IXPs.","target":"https://blog.apnic.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Korea-fig8.jpg","line":92,"embedded":true},{"title":"Korea Internet & Security Agency","target":"https://www.kisa.or.kr/EN","line":96},{"title":"Figure 9 — South Korea’s Infrastructure of subsea cables. Source: Telegeography’s Submarine Cable Map.","target":"https://blog.apnic.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Korea-fig10.jpg","line":115,"embedded":true},{"title":"Figure 10 — South Korea’s CLSs and cables.","target":"https://blog.apnic.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Korea-fig11.jpg","line":121,"embedded":true},{"title":"Figure 11 — Domestic data centres in South Korea.","target":"https://blog.apnic.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Korea-fig12.jpg","line":133,"embedded":true},{"title":"KRNOG 1.0","target":"https://blog.apnic.net/2023/05/08/event-wrap-krnog-1/","line":149},{"title":"mailing list","target":"https://blog.apnic.net/2024/03/19/the-internet-landscape-of-south-korea-and-krnog-update/krnog@googlegroups.com","line":149},{"title":"Facebook","target":"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100090917631240&mibextid=ZbWKwL","line":149},{"title":"LinkedIn","target":"https://www.linkedin.com/g